From: Bellatrix contributors
Subject: [PATCH] bwfm: say whether an EAPOL frame found a reader

A WPA association that loops - associate, wait, give up, re-scan, associate -
has three possible causes below wpa_supplicant, and they are indistinguishable
from outside the device: the EAPOL frames of the four-way handshake arrive and
are delivered, they arrive and nobody is reading that packet type, or they
never arrive at all.

rx_deliver() already computes the answer and already has the line. It was
behind D() with DEBUG 0, so it produced nothing in any of the three cases.

Make it unconditional and bound it to 32 frames, in the style of the other
bring-up milestones. IP, ARP and IPv6 stay excluded: they flood, and they have
a reader by definition.

---
--- a/workbench/devs/networks/bwfm/bwfm_dev.c
+++ b/workbench/devs/networks/bwfm/bwfm_dev.c
@@ -375,12 +375,29 @@
     }
     ReleaseSemaphore(&unit->lock);
 
-    /* IP/ARP flood the log and have a reader by definition; anything else is
-     * worth a line, because a frame nobody reads (EAPOL, say) is silently lost. */
+    /*
+     * IP/ARP flood the log and have a reader by definition; anything else is
+     * worth a line, because a frame nobody reads (EAPOL, say) is silently lost.
+     *
+     * Unconditional with DEBUG 0, and bounded, because this is the only line
+     * that can tell three states apart when a WPA association loops forever:
+     * EAPOL arriving and delivered, EAPOL arriving with nobody reading it, and
+     * EAPOL never arriving at all. The first is a working handshake path, the
+     * second a defect here, the third a defect below us. Silence looks the
+     * same for all three.
+     */
     if (packet_type != 0x0800 && packet_type != 0x0806 && packet_type != 0x86dd)
-        D(bug("[bwfm.device] type 0x%04x len %u -> %s\n",
-              (unsigned)packet_type, (unsigned)len,
-              delivered ? "opener" : "NO READER (dropped)"));
+    {
+        static ULONG shown = 0;
+
+        if (shown < 32)
+        {
+            bug("[WIFI:DEV] rx type 0x%04x len %u -> %s\n",
+                (unsigned)packet_type, (unsigned)len,
+                delivered ? "opener" : "NO READER (dropped)");
+            shown++;
+        }
+    }
 }
 
